wildos-winmode (0.3.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Save to disk is back. It was held back because a save would not load
    on a PC with the old virtiofs shared folder; the folders now travel
    over the RemoteApp connection, a Windows still carrying that share
    loses it at its next start from off, and the code that took the
    share out and put it back is gone. Windows is paused before it is
    saved and comes back running, and the connection ends as it saves,
    so Remote Desktop can't reopen the first app a second time when
    Windows comes back; a new connection brings its windows back.
  * Resume, Start, Restart and Shut down for the taskbar's Windows mode
    panel (Power on the service and the agent, "wildos-winmode power").
    Shut down goes through Windows' guest agent, else the power button,
    and Windows is switched off after 90 seconds if it hasn't finished,
    which is said. Restart is a shut down and a start from off.
  * Unsaved work: wild-guest reads Word, Excel and PowerPoint's own Saved
    state over COM ("documents"), and window titles mark it for apps
    such as Notepad. Restart and Shut down ask first when anything is,
    or might be, unsaved.
  * Shutting down, restarting or signing out of Wild OS with Windows apps
    open asks (board 9.9) through ksmserver's session management, as an
    app with unsaved work does: Keep my work saves Windows to disk and
    the next sign-in brings its apps back; after 60 seconds that is the
    choice. A PC shut down any other way with apps open saves Windows
    too, under a logind delay lock (InhibitDelayMaxSec 60).
  * The panel says how long Windows has been paused, saved or off, and
    how long it last took to start and to come back from disk.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +0000

wildos-winmode (0.3.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Windows has all the memory it is set to while any Windows app is open.
    Unused memory went back to Wild OS every 30 seconds whatever Windows
    was doing, and Windows only grew back into it a step at a time, so
    with 8 GB set it worked like a 4 GB PC: a program asking for 5 GB
    took 94 seconds to get it. Memory now goes back only while no Windows
    app is open, and the first app to open gets all of it at once,
    including one opened from inside Windows.
  * After a change of memory in Settings, an app opening before Windows
    had restarted got none of Windows' memory back: the service asked for
    the new amount, which a running Windows can't take, and libvirt
    refused the lot. It now gives back everything Windows started with,
    and the new amount comes with the restart as before.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000

wildos-winmode (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Setting up Windows mode: the wizard (boards 9.1 to 9.7) and the setup
    engine in the system service, from the steps tools/winmode-proof
    proved: download and check Windows, the answer file and payload, the
    isolated network, the virtual PC, the install, activation, tuning and
    Microsoft 365. Resumable, including after a restart.

